{
  "_comment": "Cross-section of the Study, storey by storey. Each room is a flat panel with its own image; every berth is normalized (0..1) to THAT panel, not to the house. Berths were read off the paintings themselves: a reading berth's bottom edge sits on the painted desk surface, so the card stands at the desk and the book lands on it. A berth's optional `volume` is the open book the PAINTER already put on that desk, read off the panel the same way: the card stands behind it rather than over it, so the painting keeps the piece of itself it drew there. Its optional `turn` is the patch of panel that desk's page turn is filmed over, with the clip that plays there — a wider rectangle than the volume, because a page needs somewhere to rise into, and pushed off-centre by however much it takes to keep that room's candle out of frame; see tools/occult-art/book-turns.yaml for how each was chosen. An anchor is either a room of its own kind or a `prop` standing inside somebody else's room — the parlour holds three, because a storey spent on a single prop is paid for by every card in the house.",
